<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "(Elucidation) A two-dimensional spatial region is a spatial region that is a whole consisting of a surface together with zero or more surfaces which may have spatial regions of lower dimension as parts"@en .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The surface of a sphere-shaped part of space; an infinitely thin plane in space"@en .
