# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000003
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Material Classification System"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000003> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A formal classification system allowing to identify and name EngineeredMaterials. Examples for metals include the US UNS numbering system (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unified_numbering_system), the Register of European Steels (https://stahldaten.de/stahldat-sx/stahl-eisen-liste/) and others. \n\nTODO: Possibly instatiate some relevant classifcation systems."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000004
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This class is the \"entry point\" for the multi-scale perspective on material entities by recursively consisting of Material Entity Aggregates. In particular, this class is not “disjoint” with object."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Material Entity Aggregate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material entity that is a mereological sum of separate material entities and possesses nonconnected boundaries."@en .
