# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000602> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "“Thermocouple.” Merriam-Webster.com Dictionary, Merriam-Webster, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/thermocouple. Accessed 13 Jan. 2023."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thermocouple"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thermoelement"@de .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A device for measuring temperature in which a pair of wires of dissimilar metals (such as copper and iron) are joined and the free ends of the wires are connected to an instrument (such as a voltmeter) that measures the difference in potential created at the junction of the two metals."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000983> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ein Gerät zur Temperaturmessung, bei dem ein Paar Drähte aus unterschiedlichen Metallen (z. B. Kupfer und Eisen) verbunden und die freien Enden der Drähte mit einem Instrument (z. B. einem Voltmeter) verbunden werden, das die an der Verbindungsstelle erzeugte der beiden Metalle Potentialdifferenz misst ."@de .
