_:genid714 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020098> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bravais Lattice (3D)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020099> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Bravais Lattice is a nature constant that describes the possible geometric arrangement of lattice points in a crystal. The present descriptor is limited to the 14 possible three-dimensional arrangements. \n\nTODO: possibly extend for 2D (Graphene etc)\n\nMore elaborate crystal descriptions may be found in http://emmo.info/domain-crystallography/crystallography or https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/disos/cso"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000145> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Proportion"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Proportion is a relational quality between two entites (the whole and the part) which quantifies the relation between the whole and its part."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020102
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020102> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020102> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020102> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mass Proportion"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020102> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Mass Proportion is a Proportion which quantifies the mass of the part relative to the mass of the whole."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020103
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020103> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020103> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020103> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Molar Proportion"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020103> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Molar Ratio"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020103> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Molar Proportion is the proportion which quantifies the entities count of the part in relation to the entites count of the whole."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020103> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The molar ratio of hydrogen gas H2 molecules to water H2O molecules is 1/1 in the oxyhydrogen reaction. The molar ratio of oxigen molecules O2 to water molecules is 2/1.\nThe molar ratio of carbon dioxide to average atmosphere air is 420 ppm as of 2022 AD."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020101> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Volume Proportion"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020104> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Mass Proportion is a Proportion which quantifies the volume of the part relative to the volume of the whole."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020105
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020105> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020105> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020105> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mineral"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020105> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A mineral is a material that has part some crystal."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polycrystal"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020106> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A polycrystall is an object aggregate that has continuant part some crystal grains."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020108
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020108> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020108> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020105> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020108> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Graphite"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020108> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A mineral that has part some crystal that in turn consists of some portion of carbon"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020109
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020109> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020109> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000985> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020109> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Intensive thermodynamic property"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020109> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An intensive thermodynamic property is a thermodynamic property that inheres in a portion of matter."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020110
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020110> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020110> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000985> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020110> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Extensive thermodynamic property"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020110> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extensive thermodynamic property is a thermodynamic property that inheres in an object or object aggregate where the object or object aggregate is considered the thermodynamic system."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020115
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020115> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020115> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000891> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020115> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aerosol"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020115> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An aerosol is a disconnected material entity aggregate which:\n1. consists of some portion of matter whose aggregate state quality concretizes gasous and \n2. consists of some portion of matter whose aggregate state quality concretises solid or liquid (TODO: express that this portion is also a disconnected material entity aggregate)"@en .
