<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020128> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020128> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020128> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thermodynamic system"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020128> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thermodynamic system is an object aggregate whose objects are bearer of  thermodynamic properties. A thermodynamic system environs a thermodynamic process by which the thermodynamic properties of the objects of the thermodynamic system change over time."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020129
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020129> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020129> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020129> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reversible process"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020129> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reversible process is a process whose participants form a thermodynamic system with an entropy S and S remains constant during the process."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Intensive quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Point property"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An intensive quality is a qualty that inheres in only portion of matter and thus is independent of the bearers (system-) size."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020132
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020132> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020132> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020132> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Size"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020132> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Size is the quality of a material entity that describes its spatial extend."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020133
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020133> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020133> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020133> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mass"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020133> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Mass is a quality that inheres in an object, object aggregate or fiat object part and affects those in processes where gravitation, acceleration, thermal mass etc are relevant."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020134
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020134> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020134> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020134> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Stimulus role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "See 'Stimulus role'"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020134> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The stimulus role is a role that an object bears in a process when causally influencing another object  that bears a stimulation target role in the same process."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020135
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020135> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020135> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020135> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Stimulation target role"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020138
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020138> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020138> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020138> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Lot"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020138> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A lot is an object aggregate whose parts are output of the same prodction process."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020139
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020139> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020139> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000533> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020139> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Heat (metallurgy)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020139> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A heat is a fixed amount of metallic alloy that has the disposition to be input to some Manifacturing Process."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020140
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020140> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020140> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020140> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Universal intensive quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020140> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A universal intensive quality is an intensive quality that every portion of matter bears at any point in time."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <http://openenergy-platform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00000150> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020142> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Energy is a quality of material entities which manifests as a capacity to perform work (such as causing motion or the interaction of molecules)"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020143
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020143> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020143> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020143> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Process chain"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020143> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process chain is a process that 'has contiuant part' subprocesses S1...Sn where S1...Sn precede each other and where some object or object aggregate that are output of Sn are then input to Sn+1."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020144
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020144> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020144> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020144> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Product (chemical reaction)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020144> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Product is the role of a material entity that is output of a chemical reaction and is created or transformed during the reaction."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020145
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020145> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020145> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020145> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Educt"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020145> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Educt is the role of a material entity that is input of a chemical reaction and is consumed or transformed during the reaction"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020146
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020146> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020146> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020146> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Catalyst"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020146> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Catalyst is the role of a participant in a chemical reaction that does not alter its qualities/realizable entities  after the chemical reaction."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Extensive quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An extensive quality is a qualty that inheres in only object or object aggregate or fiat object part or chemical entity and is dependent on the bearers (system-) size."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Universal extensive quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A universal extensive quality is an intensive quality that the bearer bears at any point in time."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020150
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020150> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020150> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020150> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Volume"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020150> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Volume is a universal extensive quality that affects those in processes where a spatial region/spatial extent is relevant."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020151
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020151> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020151> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020149> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020151> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Internal Energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020151> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Internal energy is a universal extensive quality that specifies the bearers potential to do work."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020152
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020152> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020152> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020152> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Component"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020152> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A component is an object aggregate that bears a function in a technical system."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020153
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020153> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020153> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020153> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Technical system"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020153> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A technical system is an object aggretate: \n1. that is output of a manufacturing process, \n2. that bears some function \n3. whose continuant parts are some components."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020154
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020154> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020154> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020154> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Atomic extensive quality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020154> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An atomic extensive quality is a extensive quality that inheres in atom aggregates."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020155
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020155> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020155> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020154> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020155> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Interatomic interaction energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020155> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Interatomic interaction energy is added/removed from the atom aggregate if one atom is moved infinitely away from the rest of the aggregate."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000145> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bond"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A bond is a relational quality describing the force interaction between atoms."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050001
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://sciencenotes.org/types-of-chemical-bonds/> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Covalent Bond"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A covalent bond is a bond that forms when nonmetal atoms share electrons to achieve a stable electron configuration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "In a water molecule (H₂O), the hydrogen and oxygen atoms share electrons."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050002
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050002> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://www.thoughtco.com/metallic-bond-definition-properties-and-examples-4117948> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Metallic Bond"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050002> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A metallic bond is a bond that forms between metal atoms, where electrons are shared in a \"sea\" of electrons that move freely around the metal ions. This type of bonding gives metals their characteristic properties such as conductivity and malleability."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050003
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050000> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050003> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> <https://sciencenotes.org/types-of-chemical-bonds/> .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ionic Bond"@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050003> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An ionic bond is a bond that occurs when one atom donates an electron to another atom, resulting in oppositely charged ions that attract each other."@en .
<https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0050003> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An example is the interaction between the atoms of sodium chloride (NaCl), where the sodium atom donates an electron to a chlorine atom."@en .
# 
